Count only effects the project still defines in the "N failing" count.

The count took the newest run of each effect and counted those that
failed. An effect that was renamed or removed never runs again, so its
last failure stayed counted for good. An effect now counts only while
the newest default-branch effects pass whose definitions evaluated lists
it (its onPush rows and checks, found by effects_branch since a merge
reuses its PR or batch build), and a scheduled effect only while its
schedule is in scheduled_effects.

